      "data": {
        "text": "**Choosing a TTS Provider**\n\nI'm now zeroing in on a Text-to-Speech provider. Google Cloud TTS seems like a solid choice for the `synthesize_text.py` script. The next step is to nail down the specific implementation details, especially how to convert the plain text into an audio byte stream.\n\n\n**Implementing the Synthesis**\n\nOkay, I've started putting together the `synthesize_text.py` file. I'm focusing on the Google Cloud Text-to-Speech integration right now. The initial code includes the import for the Google Cloud client library, and I'm instantiating the `TextToSpeechClient`. My current task is to figure out the exact method calls and parameters to convert plain text into an audio byte stream using this specific provider.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789863003951,
          "start": 1789863001377
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
      },
      "id": "prt_0bc25fd210011k4lNp8eta1diE",
